y by election you guys I wanted  to be elect you know the you know  subchapter S but at this stage these are  territorial the Congress of Honduras has  the faculty to designate an unlimited  number of special zones right now there  are two communities in Honduras  we're the local population has asked to  have it placed on the ballot in November  a few months from now if it will be  designated that there there are area  where they live will be designated as a  special jurisdiction over so so we can  look to the elections in November to see  if this stuff immediately comes online  let's say they win you know the two  places to get it you have lief  jurisdictions what happens next  well what happens next is really  exciting because what you've done is  this area is now semi-autonomous it's  separated from the political regime and  in in the in the capital there is a  Board of Trustees in essence which  provides the buffer and the guarantees  of stability under rule of law you have  into the written to the constitutional  law that there's a cap on taxation these  are low tax low regulation regimes and  the most exciting part is a page is  being taken out of the success of Lee  Kuan Yew or Hong Kong for that matter  which is Lee Kuan Yew in Singapore yeah  exactly both of those jurisdictions Hong  Kong and Singapore when Singapore came  to independence in 1965 Lee Kuan Yew  said I need to offer investors and my  population world-class justice and to  create good institutions requires time  that exceeds a human lifespan so how do  you do it what I call institutional  leapfrogging  you say okay where in the world does  that already exist well at London the  Judicial Committee of the Privy Council  members of the House of Lords with wigs  they're not going to be taking bribes  from a businessman in Singapore or a  foreign investor doing business there  that will be my Supreme Court so said  Lee Kuan Yew when he kept it that way  for 20 years Hong Kong throughout the  Britis